  "body": "## Fixed\n\n- **`nlm setup add claude-desktop` now writes to the right file on migrated Windows Store installs.** Newer Microsoft Store builds of Claude Desktop move their user data to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Claude-Data\\<package>`. We only knew the old path under `Packages\\`, so `setup add` wrote a config the app never read, and `setup list` showed a false ✓ for it. The resolver now follows the app's own rule: the new folder is used only when it exists as a directory and no `.user-data-back.<package>` marker is in the old folder. An empty `Claude-Data` next to a live old folder keeps the old path, so working installs don't change ([#378](https://github.com/jacob-bd/gemini-notebook-mcp-cli/issues/378)).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Unverified: when the new folder exists with neither a `left` nor a `back` marker, Claude Desktop runs an extra check we haven't read. We treat that case as migrated.\n\n## Credits\n\nThanks to **@diogoflorencio** for the report and the manual workaround in #378.\n",
